  Slug: paragon-benefit-regalia
  DisplayName: Paragon Benefit (Regalia)
  IconPath: icons/commodities/gems/pearl-red-gold.webp
  Description: Your regalia grants you the true gravitas of rulership, tying together
    the hearts and minds of your allies and making it impossible for you to leave
    a bad impression. If you roll a critical failure on a check to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Coerce],
    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Make an Impression], or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Request],
    you get a failure instead. When others use @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Follow
    the Expert] to follow you, you grant them a +3 circumstance bonus if you are
    trained or +4 if you are an expert or above. Allies in your inspiring aura aren't
    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Off-Guard] from being flanked unless
    you too are flanked. If one of your allies in the aura is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Clumsy],
    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Enfeebled], @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Frightened],
    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Sickened], or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Stupefied],
    the status penalty your ally takes from the condition is 1 lower than the condition's
    value as long as the ally remains in the aura, unless you too are affected by
    the same condition.
